/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kake-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-80/w1/ExecGuard.md:9:`prefix_probe` (`scripts/ledger_append_guard.py:37-45`): `cut = base.rindex(b"]")`; preserved iff `carrier.startswith(base[:cut])`; on failure reports the first divergent offset. I endorse this over the common-prefix+common-suffix (A+I+B) rule I proposed mid-wave: A+I+B would accept a mid-entry insertion (e.g. a field spliced into a prior event's note — the rewrite class R79-2 targets) as long as the tail matched, while prefix-to-`]`` accepts only an insertion at the array's end, which is exactly the sanctioned byte-splice. I could not name any legitimate append that must move bytes before the final `]` — the L1's challenge stands answered: none exists under this ledger's end-append discipline.
